6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-10-30T22:08:09Z","updated_at":"2025-11-01T04:59:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: 4.5.1\n\n### System information\n\nAny\n\n### Issue description\n\n```GDScript\nvar object = Object.new()\nobject.whatever = \"value\"\n```\nTrying to access a class property that does not exist, as in the above example, prints the following error message:\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Invalid assignment of property or key 'whatever' with value of type 'String' on a base object of type 'Object'. \n\nThis seems reasonable at first glance, however it can become confusing when combined with Dictionaries:\n```GDScript\nvar object = MyCustomObject.new()\nobject.my_custom_dictionary[\"Hellow World\"] = \"whatever\"\n```\nIf the Object in question does not have a `my_custom_dictionary` property, it will still print the same error as above, which can make one think that the property exists, but something may be wrong with the dictionary itself. See [this forum post](https://forum.godotengine.org/t/struggling-to-implement-save-load-feature/126380) as an example (of me being confused).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```GDScript\nvar object = Object.new()\nobject.whatever = \"value\"\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nn/a","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112225/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused"